spec:
  grid: 16-20 rows x 16-19 cols, background 0
  rectangles:
    count: 1-3 non-overlapping solid foreground rectangles
    size: 6-13 rows x 6-13 cols
    separation: >=1 cell gap between any two rectangles (no touching)
    may_touch_grid_edge: yes [observed]
  nested_layers:
    count: 3-5 per rectangle, each a distinct non-background color
    structure: concentric rectangular rings peeled inward; each non-innermost layer has uniform thickness on all 4 sides (symmetric)
    thickness: 1-2 cells per non-innermost layer
    innermost: fills remaining interior (not necessarily symmetric)
    color_uniqueness: all layer colors within a rectangle are distinct; colors may repeat across rectangles
  transform: reverse the order of layer colors within each rectangle (outermost swaps with innermost, etc.); background unchanged; grid size unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (no inversion needed; input is self-contained)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size in 16-20 x 16-19.
    2. Pick 1-3 rectangles with sizes 6-13 x 6-13; place them on the grid with >=1 cell gap between pairs, allowing grid-edge contact.
    3. For each rectangle, pick 3-5 distinct non-zero colors for layers.
    4. Build layers outside-in. For each non-innermost layer, pick uniform thickness 1 or 2. Ensure remaining interior after peeling is >=1x1 and can accommodate remaining layers (at least 2*remaining_layers-1 in each dimension).
    5. The innermost layer fills whatever remains.
    6. Paint layers onto the rectangle region. Fill background with 0.
```
